PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L01U3.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":1,"cefr":"A1a","unit":3,"theme":"In My Classroom","essential_question":"What do we need to learn well in our classroom?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1","title":"A Pencil, An Eraser, Two Rulers","objectives":["Students will be able to use a and an correctly before singular nouns.","Students will be able to make regular plurals with -s and -es.","I can say \"a pencil\" and \"an eraser\".","I can say \"two pencils\" and \"three boxes\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام a وan بشكل صحيح قبل الأسماء المفردة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من جمع الأسماء بإضافة s أو es.","أستطيع أن أقول a pencil وan eraser.","أستطيع أن أقول two pencils وthree boxes."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"pencil","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɛnsəl/","definition":"a thing you use to write and draw","arabic":"قلم رصاص","example":"Please sharpen your pencil.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-W01"},{"word":"eraser","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪˈreɪsɚ/","definition":"a small thing that takes away pencil marks","arabic":"ممحاة","example":"This eraser smells like strawberries.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-W02"},{"word":"ruler","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrulɚ/","definition":"a long, flat thing for drawing straight lines","arabic":"مسطرة","example":"Use a ruler to draw the line.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-W03"},{"word":"notebook","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈnoʊtˌbʊk/","definition":"a book with empty pages for writing","arabic":"دفتر","example":"Write the date in your notebook.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use a or an before ONE thing (a singular noun). Use a before a consonant sound: a pencil, a map. Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u): an eraser, an apple.\nFor two or more things, add -s: pencil → pencils. Add -es after s, ss, sh, ch, x: box → boxes, watch → watches.\nDo not use a or an with plurals: a book → books (NOT a books).\na + consonant sound: a desk, a ruler, a clock\nan + vowel sound: an eraser, an orange, an umbrella\nplural = noun + -s: chairs, maps, crayons\nplural = noun + -es after s, ss, sh, ch, x: buses, glasses, brushes, lunches, boxes","examples":["I have a ruler.","She needs an eraser.","There are four chairs at our table.","The maps are on the wall.","Two boxes are full of paper.","Is that an orange crayon?","Our teacher has three watches.","Adam eats an apple at break time."],"common_errors":["✗ I have pencil. → ✓ I have a pencil. (Arabic has no word for \"a\"; English needs a/an before one thing.)","✗ She has a eraser. → ✓ She has an eraser. (eraser starts with a vowel sound → an.)","✗ I have two book. → ✓ I have two books. (After two, three… add -s.)","✗ three boxs → ✓ three boxes (After x, add -es.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم a أو an قبل الاسم المفرد: a pencil، وan قبل الاسم الذي يبدأ بصوت متحرك: an eraser.\nفي العربية لا توجد كلمة تقابل a، لكن في الإنجليزية لا بد منها قبل المفرد: I have a pencil.\nللجمع نضيف s: pencils، ونضيف es بعد s وsh وch وx: boxes.\nلا نستخدم a مع الجمع: books وليس a books."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Pencil, An Eraser, Two Rulers”. Let’s learn a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U3-LS1 | A Pencil, An Eraser, Two Rulers","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Our Classroom”: Welcome to Class 3A! Our classroom is big and bright. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Welcome to Class 3A! Our classroom is big and bright.","visual":"Image GV-L01-U3-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use a or an before ONE thing (a singular noun). Use a before a consonant sound: a pencil, a map. Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u): an eraser, an apple. For two or more things, add -s: pencil → pencils. Add -es after s, ss, sh, ch, x: box → boxes, watch → watches.","on_screen":"a + consonant sound: a desk, a ruler, a clock • an + vowel sound: an eraser, an orange, an umbrella • plural = noun + -s: chairs, maps, crayons","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I have a ruler. She needs an eraser. There are four chairs at our table.","on_screen":"I have a ruler. / She needs an eraser. / There are four chairs at our table.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I have pencil.” That’s not right. We say: “I have a pencil.” Arabic has no word for \"a\"; English needs a/an before one thing.","on_screen":"✗ I have pencil.   ✓ I have a pencil.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"an eraser\" – one eraser or many? … Think! … One. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"a pencil\" and \"an eraser\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"a pencil\" and \"an eraser\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم a أو an قبل الاسم المفرد: a pencil، وan قبل الاسم الذي يبدأ بصوت متحرك: an eraser.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I have pencil. — الصحيح: I have a pencil.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول a pencil وan eraser."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Our Classroom","body":"Welcome to Class 3A! Our classroom is big and bright.\nOn the wall is a map and a clock. My desk is next to a window.\nOn my desk is a notebook, an eraser and two pencils.\nOmar's crayons are in a box. Yusuf's glue sticks are in his bag.\nMr. Khalid's desk is near the board. On it are three books and an apple.\nI like my classroom!","word_count":69,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"I need ___ ruler.","options":["an","two","a","some"],"answer":"a","explanation":"Use a before a consonant sound.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم a قبل الصوت الساكن."},{"q":"Lina has ___ umbrella.","options":["an","the a","two","a"],"answer":"an","explanation":"Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم an قبل الصوت المتحرك."},{"q":"Can I have ___ glue stick, please?","options":["an","two","the an","a"],"answer":"a","explanation":"Use a before a consonant sound.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم a قبل الصوت الساكن."},{"q":"There are five ___ in the box.","options":["crayones","crayons","crayon","a crayon"],"answer":"crayons","explanation":"For two or more, add -s.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نضيف s."},{"q":"Two ___ are on the teacher's desk.","options":["watches","watchs","watch","a watch"],"answer":"watches","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch or x, add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."},{"q":"Look! It's ___ owl in the tree.","options":["two","a","owls","an"],"answer":"an","explanation":"Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم an قبل الصوت المتحرك."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write a or an. Word bank: a, an","items":[{"q":"Yusuf has ______ orange bag.","options":[],"answer":"an","explanation":"Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم an قبل الصوت المتحرك."},{"q":"This is ______ blue notebook.","options":[],"answer":"a","explanation":"Use a before a consonant sound.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم a قبل الصوت الساكن."},{"q":"I see ______ egg in the picture.","options":[],"answer":"an","explanation":"Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم an قبل الصوت المتحرك."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the plural.","items":[{"q":"one bus  (plural)","options":[],"answer":"two buses","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch or x, add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."},{"q":"one desk  (plural)","options":[],"answer":"three desks","explanation":"For two or more, add -s.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نضيف s."},{"q":"one brush  (plural)","options":[],"answer":"four brushes","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch or x, add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Look around your classroom. Complete the sentences.","items":[{"q":"On my desk, I have a ___.","options":[],"answer":"On my desk, I have a ruler.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In my bag, I have an ___.","options":[],"answer":"In my bag, I have an eraser.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In our classroom there are ___ windows.","options":[],"answer":"There are three windows.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My friend has two ___.","options":[],"answer":"My friend has two pencils.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I can see a ___ and a ___ on the wall.","options":[],"answer":"I can see a map and a clock on the wall.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write and count.","items":[{"q":"Write a list of 5 things in your bag with a, an or numbers.","options":[],"answer":"a notebook, an eraser, two pencils, three crayons, a ruler","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your classroom.","options":[],"answer":"Our classroom has a big board. There are two doors. I can see an old clock.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask your partner: \"What's in your pencil case?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"He has a pencil, an eraser and two pens.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin & Speak","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Work in teams of four. Player 1 spins the wheel.","Make a correct sentence about the unit theme using the cue word and a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es).","The team checks the sentence with the grammar box. Correct = 1 point; an extra detail = 1 bonus point.","Pass the spinner clockwise. Play for 6 minutes; the team with most points wins."],"data":[{"label":"a pencil"},{"label":"an eraser"},{"label":"two rulers"},{"label":"a notebook"},{"label":"three boxes"},{"label":"an apple"},{"label":"a clock"},{"label":"five crayons"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I have ___ notebook.","options":["a","two","some","an"],"answer":"a","explanation":"Use a before a consonant sound.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم a قبل الصوت الساكن."},{"q":"She needs ___ eraser.","options":["an","some","a","two"],"answer":"an","explanation":"Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم an قبل الصوت المتحرك."},{"q":"Look at those three ___.","options":["a bus","buss","buses","bus"],"answer":"buses","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch or x, add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."},{"q":"There are six ___ in our room.","options":["a chair","chairs","chaires","chair"],"answer":"chairs","explanation":"For two or more, add -s.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نضيف s."},{"q":"Is it ___ apple or a banana?","options":["a","the a","two","an"],"answer":"an","explanation":"Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم an قبل الصوت المتحرك."},{"q":"","options":["I have a maps.","I have two maps.","I have two map.","I have two mapes."],"answer":"I have two maps.","explanation":"Don't use a/an with plurals.","explanation_ar":"لا نستخدم a أو an مع الجمع."},{"q":"We need ___ clock for the wall.","options":["clocks","a","an","two"],"answer":"a","explanation":"Use a before a consonant sound.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم a قبل الصوت الساكن."},{"q":"The teacher has two ___.","options":["boxes","a box","boxs","box"],"answer":"boxes","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch or x, add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."},{"q":"","options":["Omar eats orange.","Omar eats a orange.","Omar eats an oranges.","Omar eats an orange."],"answer":"Omar eats an orange.","explanation":"Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم an قبل الصوت المتحرك."},{"q":"Which plural is correct?","options":["lunchies","lunchs","lunches","lunch"],"answer":"lunches","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch or x, add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"A bright classroom with a world map and a clock on the wall; on a desk a notebook, an eraser and two pencils, a box of crayons and an apple on the teacher's desk. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A bright classroom with a world map and a clock on the wall; on a desk a notebook, an eraser and two pencils, a box of crayons and an apple on the teacher's desk"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows pencil (a thing you use to write and draw); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing pencil: a thing you use to write and draw"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows eraser (a small thing that takes away pencil marks); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing eraser: a small thing that takes away pencil marks"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows ruler (a long, flat thing for drawing straight lines); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing ruler: a long, flat thing for drawing straight lines"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows notebook (a book with empty pages for writing); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing notebook: a book with empty pages for writing"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin & Speak”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin & Speak"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-W01","script":"pencil. pencil. Please sharpen your pencil.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-W02","script":"eraser. eraser. This eraser smells like strawberries.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-W03","script":"ruler. ruler. Use a ruler to draw the line.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-W04","script":"notebook. notebook. Write the date in your notebook.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-T1","script":"Welcome to Class 3A! Our classroom is big and bright. On the wall is a map and a clock. My desk is next to a window. On my desk is a notebook, an eraser and two pencils. Omar's crayons are in a box. Yusuf's glue sticks are in his bag. Mr. Khalid's desk is near the board. On it are three books and an apple. I like my classroom!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Pencil, An Eraser, Two Rulers”. Let’s learn a / an and regular plurals (-s, -es) together. Listen to the start of “Our Classroom”: Welcome to Class 3A! Our classroom is big and bright. Look at the green words. Use a or an before ONE thing (a singular noun). Use a before a consonant sound: a pencil, a map. Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u): an eraser, an apple. For two or more things, add -s: pencil → pencils. Add -es after s, ss, sh, ch, x: box → boxes, watch → watches. Here are some examples. I have a ruler. She needs an eraser. There are four chairs at our table. Be careful! Some learners say: “I have pencil.” That’s not right. We say: “I have a pencil.” Arabic has no word for \"a\"; English needs a/an before one thing. Quick check: \"an eraser\" – one eraser or many? … Think! … One. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"a pencil\" and \"an eraser\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2","title":"This, That, These, Those","objectives":["Students will be able to use this and these for things near them and that and those for things far away.","Students will be able to match this/that with singular nouns and these/those with plural nouns.","I can say \"This is my pencil\" and \"Those are my books\".","I can ask \"What's that?\" and \"What are these?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام this وthese للقريب وthat وthose للبعيد.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام this/that مع المفرد وthese/those مع الجمع.","أستطيع أن أقول This is my pencil وThose are my books.","أستطيع أن أسأل What's that? وWhat are these?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"desk","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɛsk/","definition":"a table where you sit and work at school","arabic":"مكتب / طاولة الطالب","example":"My desk is next to the door.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS2-W01"},{"word":"chair","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tʃɛr/","definition":"a seat with a back for one person","arabic":"كرسي","example":"Push in your chair, please.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS2-W02"},{"word":"board","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bɔrd/","definition":"a big flat surface on the wall for writing","arabic":"سبورة","example":"The teacher writes new words on the board.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS2-W03"},{"word":"crayon","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkreɪˌɑn/","definition":"a stick of colored wax for drawing","arabic":"قلم تلوين شمعي","example":"The green crayon is broken.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use this (one) and these (many) for things near you – you can touch them.\nUse that (one) and those (many) for things far from you – you point to them.\nthis/that + is + singular noun; these/those + are + plural noun.","examples":["This is my new eraser.","These are Sara's crayons.","That is the school library.","Those are our science books.","What's that on the wall? – It's a map.","Are these your scissors? – Yes, they are.","This glue stick is empty.","Those boys are in Class 3C."],"common_errors":["✗ This are my books. → ✓ These are my books. (books is plural → these … are.)","✗ What is these? → ✓ What are these? (these is plural → are.)","✗ Those is a clock. → ✓ That is a clock. (one far thing → that.)"],"arabic":"this = هذا/هذه (للقريب المفرد)، these = هؤلاء/هذه (للقريب الجمع).\nthat = ذلك/تلك (للبعيد المفرد)، those = أولئك/تلك (للبعيد الجمع).\nthis وthat مع is والمفرد، وthese وthose مع are والجمع."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “This, That, These, Those”. Let’s learn demonstratives this / that / these / those together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U3-LS2 | This, That, These, Those","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: This is a pencil. • These are pencils. • That is a clock. • Those are maps. This isn't my bag. • Those aren't our crayons. What's this? – It's a ruler. • What are those? – They're scissors.","on_screen":"This is a pencil. • These are pencils. • That is a clock. • Those are maps. | This isn't my bag. • Those aren't our crayons. | What's this? – It's a ruler. • What are those? – They're scissors.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use this (one) and these (many) for things near you – you can touch them. Use that (one) and those (many) for things far from you – you point to them.","on_screen":"demonstratives this / that / these / those","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. This is my new eraser. These are Sara's crayons. That is the school library.","on_screen":"This is my new eraser. / These are Sara's crayons. / That is the school library.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “This are my books.” That’s not right. We say: “These are my books.” books is plural → these … are.","on_screen":"✗ This are my books.   ✓ These are my books.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: The book is in my hand. This or that? … Think! … *This* – it is near. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"This is my pencil\" and \"Those are my books\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"This is my pencil\" and \"Those are my books\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: demonstratives this / that / these / those.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","this = هذا/هذه (للقريب المفرد)، these = هؤلاء/هذه (للقريب الجمع).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: This are my books. — الصحيح: These are my books.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول This is my pencil وThose are my books."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"(in my hand) ___ is my ruler.","options":["These","This","Those","That are"],"answer":"This","explanation":"Near + one → this.","explanation_ar":"قريب ومفرد ← this."},{"q":"(far away) ___ are the school buses.","options":["This","That","Those","These is"],"answer":"Those","explanation":"Far + many → those.","explanation_ar":"بعيد وجمع ← those."},{"q":"(near me) ___ are my new crayons.","options":["That","This","These","Those is"],"answer":"These","explanation":"Near + many → these.","explanation_ar":"قريب وجمع ← these."},{"q":"(on the far wall) ___ is a big map.","options":["Those","This are","These","That"],"answer":"That","explanation":"Far + one → that.","explanation_ar":"بعيد ومفرد ← that."},{"q":"What ___ these?","options":["are","am","is","be"],"answer":"are","explanation":"this/that + is; these/those + are.","explanation_ar":"this وthat مع is، وthese وthose مع are."},{"q":"___ is my brother over there.","options":["These","That","This are","Those"],"answer":"That","explanation":"Far + one → that.","explanation_ar":"بعيد ومفرد ← that."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Look and write this, that, these or those. Word bank: Those, These, This","items":[{"q":"(near, one) ______ chair is broken.","options":[],"answer":"This","explanation":"Near + one → this.","explanation_ar":"قريب ومفرد ← this."},{"q":"(far, many) ______ trees are tall.","options":[],"answer":"Those","explanation":"Far + many → those.","explanation_ar":"بعيد وجمع ← those."},{"q":"(near, many) ______ cookies are delicious.","options":[],"answer":"These","explanation":"Near + many → these.","explanation_ar":"قريب وجمع ← these."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make a question.","items":[{"q":"That is a clock.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Is that a clock?","explanation":"this/that + is; these/those + are.","explanation_ar":"this وthat مع is، وthese وthose مع are."},{"q":"These are your notebooks.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Are these your notebooks?","explanation":"this/that + is; these/those + are.","explanation_ar":"this وthat مع is، وthese وthose مع are."},{"q":"Those are Adam's scissors.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Are those Adam's scissors?","explanation":"this/that + is; these/those + are.","explanation_ar":"this وthat مع is، وthese وthose مع are."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Point and say. Then write.","items":[{"q":"Point to something near you. Write: This is ___.","options":[],"answer":"This is my pencil case.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses demonstratives this / that / these / those correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Point to things near you. Write: These are ___.","options":[],"answer":"These are my crayons.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses demonstratives this / that / these / those correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Point to something far away. Write: That is ___.","options":[],"answer":"That is the door.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses demonstratives this / that / these / those correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Point to things far away. Write: Those are ___.","options":[],"answer":"Those are our bags.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses demonstratives this / that / these / those correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask your partner: \"What's that?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"It's a clock.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses demonstratives this / that / these / those correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Play \"What's this?\" and write.","items":[{"q":"Put 3 things in a bag. Your partner touches one and asks \"What's this?\" Write 3 answers.","options":[],"answer":"This is a glue stick. This is a ruler. These are crayons.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses demonstratives this / that / these / those correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 questions with that or those about things in the classroom.","options":[],"answer":"What's that on the shelf? Are those Omar's books?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses demonstratives this / that / these / those correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Draw your desk. Label 4 things with this/these.","options":[],"answer":"This is my notebook. These are my pencils.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses demonstratives this / that / these / those correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Tic-Tac-Grammar","mechanic":"tic_tac_toe","rules":["Two teams: X and O. Team X chooses a square.","Using the cue, the team says a correct sentence with demonstratives this / that / these / those (the form in brackets: +, – or ?).","If the class and teacher agree it is correct, the team marks the square.","Three squares in a row wins. Play a second round with the grid turned around."],"data":[{"cue":"this / ruler / +"},{"cue":"that / map / ?"},{"cue":"these / crayons / +"},{"cue":"those / chairs / –"},{"cue":"this / eraser / ?"},{"cue":"that / clock / +"},{"cue":"these / notebooks / ?"},{"cue":"those / boxes / +"},{"cue":"this / bag / –"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___ is my eraser. (in my hand)","options":["That are","Those","These","This"],"answer":"This","explanation":"Near + one → this.","explanation_ar":"قريب ومفرد ← this."},{"q":"___ are our classroom windows. (far)","options":["That","This","These is","Those"],"answer":"Those","explanation":"Far + many → those.","explanation_ar":"بعيد وجمع ← those."},{"q":"What's ___? (far, one) – It's the clock.","options":["that","these","those","they"],"answer":"that","explanation":"Far + one → that.","explanation_ar":"بعيد ومفرد ← that."},{"q":"___ apples are red. (near, many)","options":["This","These","Is","That"],"answer":"These","explanation":"Near + many → these.","explanation_ar":"قريب وجمع ← these."},{"q":"","options":["Those is my scissors.","These are my scissors.","These is my scissors.","This are my scissors."],"answer":"These are my scissors.","explanation":"this/that + is; these/those + are.","explanation_ar":"this وthat مع is، وthese وthose مع are."},{"q":"Are those your crayons? – Yes, ___ are.","options":["it","that","those","they"],"answer":"they","explanation":"this/that + is; these/those + are.","explanation_ar":"this وthat مع is، وthese وthose مع are."},{"q":"","options":["What those are?","What is those?","What are those?","What are that?"],"answer":"What are those?","explanation":"this/that + is; these/those + are.","explanation_ar":"this وthat مع is، وthese وthose مع are."},{"q":"(near, one) ___ notebook is new.","options":["These","They","This","Those"],"answer":"This","explanation":"Near + one → this.","explanation_ar":"قريب ومفرد ← this."},{"q":"","options":["That is our teacher's car.","These is our teacher's car.","Those is our teacher's car.","That are our teacher's car."],"answer":"That is our teacher's car.","explanation":"Far + one → that.","explanation_ar":"بعيد ومفرد ← that."},{"q":"Which pair is correct?","options":["that book – these book","this book – these books","those book – that books","this books – these book"],"answer":"this book – these books","explanation":"this/that + is; these/those + are.","explanation_ar":"this وthat مع is، وthese وthose مع are."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Adam holding scissors close to him and pointing to crayons far away on a shelf; a speech bubble with \"this\" near him and \"those\" far away. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Adam holding scissors close to him and pointing to crayons far away on a shelf; a speech bubble with \"this\" near him and \"those\" far away"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of demonstratives this / that / these / those: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “In My Classroom”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of demonstratives this / that / these / those: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “In My Classroom”"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows desk (a table where you sit and work at school); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing desk: a table where you sit and work at school"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows chair (a seat with a back for one person); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing chair: a seat with a back for one person"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows board (a big flat surface on the wall for writing); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing board: a big flat surface on the wall for writing"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows crayon (a stick of colored wax for drawing); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing crayon: a stick of colored wax for drawing"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Tic-Tac-Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Tic-Tac-Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS2-W01","script":"desk. desk. My desk is next to the door.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS2-W02","script":"chair. chair. Push in your chair, please.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS2-W03","script":"board. board. The teacher writes new words on the board.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS2-W04","script":"crayon. crayon. The green crayon is broken.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “This, That, These, Those”. Let’s learn demonstratives this / that / these / those together. Remember these patterns: This is a pencil. • These are pencils. • That is a clock. • Those are maps. This isn't my bag. • Those aren't our crayons. What's this? – It's a ruler. • What are those? – They're scissors. Use this (one) and these (many) for things near you – you can touch them. Use that (one) and those (many) for things far from you – you point to them. Here are some examples. This is my new eraser. These are Sara's crayons. That is the school library. Be careful! Some learners say: “This are my books.” That’s not right. We say: “These are my books.” books is plural → these … are. Quick check: The book is in my hand. This or that? … Think! … *This* – it is near. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"This is my pencil\" and \"Those are my books\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3","title":"Classroom Things and Colors","objectives":["Students will be able to name classroom objects and describe them with colors.","Students will be able to use always-plural nouns like scissors with are.","I can name things in my classroom and say their colors.","I can say \"The scissors are…\" and \"a pair of scissors\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تسمية أدوات الصف ووصفها بالألوان.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الأسماء التي تأتي جمعًا دائمًا مثل scissors مع are.","أستطيع أن أسمّي أشياء صفي وأذكر ألوانها.","أستطيع أن أقول The scissors are… وa pair of scissors."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"scissors","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsɪzɚz/","definition":"a tool with two blades for cutting paper","arabic":"مقص","example":"Be careful with the scissors!","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS3-W01"},{"word":"glue stick","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡlu stɪk/","definition":"a stick of glue for sticking paper","arabic":"أصبع صمغ","example":"I need a glue stick for my poster.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS3-W02"},{"word":"clock","pos":"noun","ipa":"/klɑk/","definition":"a thing on the wall that shows the time","arabic":"ساعة حائط","example":"The clock says ten o'clock.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS3-W03"},{"word":"map","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mæp/","definition":"a picture that shows countries, cities and roads","arabic":"خريطة","example":"Find Taif on the map.","image_id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Classroom words help us ask for things politely: Can I have the scissors, please?\nColors come before the noun in English: a red pencil (NOT a pencil red). Colors do not change for plurals: red pencils.\nSome nouns are always plural: scissors, glasses, pants (US). Use are and a pair of: These scissors are sharp. I need a pair of scissors.\nCollocations/phrases: red • blue • yellow • green • orange • purple • pink • brown • black • white • gray (American spelling) | a red pencil • blue notebooks • a gray clock | always plural: scissors, glasses, pants → a pair of scissors | Can I have…, please? • Here you are. • Thank you.","examples":["My notebook is purple.","The board is white and clean.","Can I have a yellow crayon, please?","These scissors are sharp.","I need a pair of scissors.","Put your chair under your desk.","The clock is above the door.","The big map shows Saudi Arabia."],"common_errors":["✗ a pencil red → ✓ a red pencil (In English, the color comes before the noun.)","✗ The scissors is on the table. → ✓ The scissors are on the table. (scissors is always plural → are.)","✗ two reds pencils → ✓ two red pencils (Colors never take -s.)","✗ grey (British spelling) → ✓ gray (American English spells it gray.)"],"arabic":"في الإنجليزية يأتي اللون قبل الاسم: a red pencil (قلم أحمر).\nاللون لا يُجمع: red pencils وليس reds pencils.\nكلمة scissors (مقص) جمع دائمًا فنقول: The scissors are… أو a pair of scissors."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Classroom Things and Colors”. Let’s learn classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U3-LS3 | Classroom Things and Colors","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. scissors: a tool with two blades for cutting paper. glue stick: a stick of glue for sticking paper. clock: a thing on the wall that shows the time.","on_screen":"scissors | glue stick | clock","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Classroom words help us ask for things politely: Can I have the scissors, please? Colors come before the noun in English: a red pencil (NOT a pencil red). Colors do not change for plurals: red pencils.","on_screen":"classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My notebook is purple. The board is white and clean. Can I have a yellow crayon, please?","on_screen":"My notebook is purple. / The board is white and clean. / Can I have a yellow crayon, please?","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “a pencil red.” That’s not right. We say: “a red pencil.” In English, the color comes before the noun.","on_screen":"✗ a pencil red   ✓ a red pencil","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we say \"a pencil red\" or \"a red pencil\"? … Think! … A red pencil. Great job! Now you can say: I can name things in my classroom and say their colors.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can name things in my classroom and say their colors.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","في الإنجليزية يأتي اللون قبل الاسم: a red pencil (قلم أحمر).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: a pencil red — الصحيح: a red pencil","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسمّي أشياء صفي وأذكر ألوانها."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"We cut paper with ___.","options":["a map","a clock","scissors","a ruler"],"answer":"scissors","explanation":"Think about what we use the thing for.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في استخدام الأداة."},{"q":"The teacher writes on the ___.","options":["crayon","chair","board","eraser"],"answer":"board","explanation":"Think about what we use the thing for.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في استخدام الأداة."},{"q":"I draw a straight line with a ___.","options":["clock","ruler","glue stick","door"],"answer":"ruler","explanation":"Think about what we use the thing for.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في استخدام الأداة."},{"q":"I want a ___.","options":["crayon blue","blue crayon","blues crayon","crayon blues"],"answer":"blue crayon","explanation":"The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."},{"q":"The scissors ___ on my desk.","options":["are","am","be","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"scissors / glasses / pants are always plural → are, a pair of.","explanation_ar":"هذه الكلمات جمع دائمًا."},{"q":"Can I have the glue stick, ___?","options":["hello","yes","thank you","please"],"answer":"please","explanation":"Ask politely: Can I have…, please?","explanation_ar":"اطلب بأدب: Can I have…, please?"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to its use.","items":[{"q":"eraser","options":["we sit on it","takes away pencil marks","has empty pages for writing","shows countries and cities","sticks paper together","tells us the time"],"answer":"takes away pencil marks","explanation":"eraser → takes away pencil marks. The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."},{"q":"clock","options":["we sit on it","takes away pencil marks","has empty pages for writing","shows countries and cities","sticks paper together","tells us the time"],"answer":"tells us the time","explanation":"clock → tells us the time. The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."},{"q":"notebook","options":["we sit on it","takes away pencil marks","has empty pages for writing","shows countries and cities","sticks paper together","tells us the time"],"answer":"has empty pages for writing","explanation":"notebook → has empty pages for writing. The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."},{"q":"map","options":["we sit on it","takes away pencil marks","has empty pages for writing","shows countries and cities","sticks paper together","tells us the time"],"answer":"shows countries and cities","explanation":"map → shows countries and cities. The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."},{"q":"glue stick","options":["we sit on it","takes away pencil marks","has empty pages for writing","shows countries and cities","sticks paper together","tells us the time"],"answer":"sticks paper together","explanation":"glue stick → sticks paper together. The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."},{"q":"chair","options":["we sit on it","takes away pencil marks","has empty pages for writing","shows countries and cities","sticks paper together","tells us the time"],"answer":"we sit on it","explanation":"chair → we sit on it. The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Describe your things.","items":[{"q":"My pencil case is ___.","options":[],"answer":"My pencil case is blue.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My favorite crayon is ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite crayon is green.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Our classroom door is ___.","options":[],"answer":"Our classroom door is brown.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I have a ___ notebook and a ___ ruler.","options":[],"answer":"I have a red notebook and a yellow ruler.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask your partner for something politely. Write what you say.","options":[],"answer":"Can I have your eraser, please?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a \"My Classroom\" picture dictionary.","items":[{"q":"Draw 4 classroom things. Write the word and the color.","options":[],"answer":"a black clock, a white board, a green chair, an orange crayon","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences with colors.","options":[],"answer":"My bag is red. The map is big. My scissors are yellow.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a polite dialogue (2 lines) asking for scissors.","options":[],"answer":"Can I have the scissors, please? – Here you are.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"pencil","match":"a thing you use to write and draw","arabic":"قلم رصاص"},{"word":"eraser","match":"a small thing that takes away pencil marks","arabic":"ممحاة"},{"word":"ruler","match":"a long, flat thing for drawing straight lines","arabic":"مسطرة"},{"word":"notebook","match":"a book with empty pages for writing","arabic":"دفتر"},{"word":"desk","match":"a table where you sit and work at school","arabic":"مكتب / طاولة الطالب"},{"word":"chair","match":"a seat with a back for one person","arabic":"كرسي"},{"word":"board","match":"a big flat surface on the wall for writing","arabic":"سبورة"},{"word":"crayon","match":"a stick of colored wax for drawing","arabic":"قلم تلوين شمعي"},{"word":"scissors","match":"a tool with two blades for cutting paper","arabic":"مقص"},{"word":"glue stick","match":"a stick of glue for sticking paper","arabic":"أصبع صمغ"},{"word":"clock","match":"a thing on the wall that shows the time","arabic":"ساعة حائط"},{"word":"map","match":"a picture that shows countries, cities and roads","arabic":"خريطة"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"We stick paper with a ___.","options":["map","ruler","clock","glue stick"],"answer":"glue stick","explanation":"Think about what we use the thing for.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في استخدام الأداة."},{"q":"The ___ shows the time.","options":["desk","board","chair","clock"],"answer":"clock","explanation":"Think about what we use the thing for.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في استخدام الأداة."},{"q":"","options":["I have an eraser green.","I have a green eraser.","I have a greens eraser.","I have green an eraser."],"answer":"I have a green eraser.","explanation":"The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."},{"q":"These scissors ___ new.","options":["are","am","is","be"],"answer":"are","explanation":"scissors / glasses / pants are always plural → are, a pair of.","explanation_ar":"هذه الكلمات جمع دائمًا."},{"q":"I need ___ scissors.","options":["a pair of","an","a","one"],"answer":"a pair of","explanation":"scissors / glasses / pants are always plural → are, a pair of.","explanation_ar":"هذه الكلمات جمع دائمًا."},{"q":"We write the date in our ___.","options":["map","clock","notebook","scissors"],"answer":"notebook","explanation":"Think about what we use the thing for.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في استخدام الأداة."},{"q":"American spelling:","options":["grey","gray","greigh","graey"],"answer":"gray","explanation":"The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."},{"q":"Can I have a pencil, please? – ___","options":["I'm tired.","Goodbye.","Here you are.","Good night."],"answer":"Here you are.","explanation":"Ask politely: Can I have…, please?","explanation_ar":"اطلب بأدب: Can I have…, please?"},{"q":"","options":["Two purple crayon is on the floor.","Two crayons purple are on the floor.","Two purple crayons are on the floor.","Two purples crayons are on the floor."],"answer":"Two purple crayons are on the floor.","explanation":"The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."},{"q":"We sit at a ___ in class.","options":["desk","map","board","clock"],"answer":"desk","explanation":"Think about what we use the thing for.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في استخدام الأداة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"An open pencil case with colorful items: a red pencil, a blue eraser, a yellow ruler, green crayons, a purple glue stick and a pair of orange scissors. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"An open pencil case with colorful items: a red pencil, a blue eraser, a yellow ruler, green crayons, a purple glue stick and a pair of orange scissors"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows scissors (a tool with two blades for cutting paper); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing scissors: a tool with two blades for cutting paper"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows glue stick (a stick of glue for sticking paper); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing glue stick: a stick of glue for sticking paper"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows clock (a thing on the wall that shows the time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing clock: a thing on the wall that shows the time"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows map (a picture that shows countries, cities and roads); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing map: a picture that shows countries, cities and roads"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS3-W01","script":"scissors. scissors. Be careful with the scissors!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS3-W02","script":"glue stick. glue stick. I need a glue stick for my poster.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS3-W03","script":"clock. clock. The clock says ten o'clock.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS3-W04","script":"map. map. Find Taif on the map.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Classroom Things and Colors”. Let’s learn classroom vocabulary, colors and always-plural nouns together. Meet some new words. scissors: a tool with two blades for cutting paper. glue stick: a stick of glue for sticking paper. clock: a thing on the wall that shows the time. Classroom words help us ask for things politely: Can I have the scissors, please? Colors come before the noun in English: a red pencil (NOT a pencil red). Colors do not change for plurals: red pencils. Here are some examples. My notebook is purple. The board is white and clean. Can I have a yellow crayon, please? Be careful! Some learners say: “a pencil red.” That’s not right. We say: “a red pencil.” In English, the color comes before the noun. Quick check: Do we say \"a pencil red\" or \"a red pencil\"? … Think! … A red pencil. Great job! Now you can say: I can name things in my classroom and say their colors.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS4","title":"Asking or Telling? Question Marks and Periods","objectives":["Students will be able to end telling sentences with a period and questions with a question mark.","Students will be able to tell the difference between a telling sentence and a question.","I can put a period at the end of a telling sentence.","I can put a question mark at the end of a question."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من إنهاء الجملة الخبرية بنقطة والسؤال بعلامة استفهام.","سيتمكن الطلاب من التمييز بين الجملة الخبرية والسؤال.","أستطيع أن أضع نقطة في نهاية الجملة الخبرية.","أستطيع أن أضع علامة استفهام في نهاية السؤال."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"pencil","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɛnsəl/","definition":"a thing you use to write and draw","arabic":"قلم رصاص","example":"Please sharpen your pencil.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"eraser","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪˈreɪsɚ/","definition":"a small thing that takes away pencil marks","arabic":"ممحاة","example":"This eraser smells like strawberries.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ruler","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrulɚ/","definition":"a long, flat thing for drawing straight lines","arabic":"مسطرة","example":"Use a ruler to draw the line.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"notebook","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈnoʊtˌbʊk/","definition":"a book with empty pages for writing","arabic":"دفتر","example":"Write the date in your notebook.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"desk","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɛsk/","definition":"a table where you sit and work at school","arabic":"مكتب / طاولة الطالب","example":"My desk is next to the door.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"chair","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tʃɛr/","definition":"a seat with a back for one person","arabic":"كرسي","example":"Push in your chair, please.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A telling sentence gives information. It ends with a period (.): This is my ruler.\nA question asks for information. It ends with a question mark (?): Is this your ruler?\nQuestions often start with Is, Are, Am, What, Who, Whose, Where or How. In Arabic the question mark looks like this: ؟ – in English it faces the other way: ?\nTelling sentence → period (.): The map is big.\nQuestion → question mark (?): Is the map big?\nQuestions often start with: Is, Are, What, Who, Whose, Where, How.\nEvery sentence starts with a capital letter.","examples":["Where is my eraser?","It is under the chair.","What color is your bag?","My bag is orange.","Are these your crayons?","Who is your teacher?","The clock is on the wall.","How old is your brother?"],"common_errors":["✗ Is this your bag. → ✓ Is this your bag? (It is a question → question mark.)","✗ What is your name؟ → ✓ What is your name? (Use the English question mark (?), not the Arabic one (؟).)","✗ my pencil is red? → ✓ My pencil is red. (It is a telling sentence → capital letter and period.)"],"arabic":"الجملة الخبرية تنتهي بنقطة (.) والسؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام (?).\nانتبه: علامة الاستفهام الإنجليزية (?) تتجه عكس العربية (؟).\nكثير من الأسئلة تبدأ بـ Is أو Are أو What أو Who أو Where."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Asking or Telling? Question Marks and Periods”. Let’s learn end punctuation: question mark (?) and period (.) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U3-LS4 | Asking or Telling? Question Marks and Periods","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A telling sentence gives information. It ends with a period (.): This is my ruler.","on_screen":"end punctuation: question mark (?) and period (.)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A telling sentence gives information. It ends with a period (.): This is my ruler. A question asks for information. It ends with a question mark (?): Is this your ruler?","on_screen":"Telling sentence → period (.): The map is big. • Question → question mark (?): Is the map big? • Questions often start with: Is, Are, What, Who, Whose, Where, How.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Where is my eraser? It is under the chair. What color is your bag?","on_screen":"Where is my eraser? / It is under the chair. / What color is your bag?","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Is this your bag.” That’s not right. We say: “Is this your bag?.” It is a question → question mark.","on_screen":"✗ Is this your bag.   ✓ Is this your bag?","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Where is the map\" – telling or asking? Which mark? … Think! … Asking – a question mark. Great job! Now you can say: I can put a period at the end of a telling sentence.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can put a period at the end of a telling sentence.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: end punctuation: question mark (?) and period (.).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الجملة الخبرية تنتهي بنقطة (.) والسؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام (?).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Is this your bag. — الصحيح: Is this your bag?","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أضع نقطة في نهاية الجملة الخبرية."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"At the Classroom Door (editing passage)","body":"Omar: where is my ruler? Yusuf: It is on your desk Omar: Is it red. Yusuf: No, it is blue. Omar: Thank you? yusuf is a good friend.","word_count":28,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["Is this your notebook.","Is this your notebook?","Is this your notebook","is this your notebook?"],"answer":"Is this your notebook?","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"","options":["The board is white.","The board is white","The board is white?","the board is white."],"answer":"The board is white.","explanation":"A telling sentence ends with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"الجملة الخبرية تنتهي بنقطة."},{"q":"","options":["Where is the clock","where is the clock?","Where is the clock.","Where is the clock?"],"answer":"Where is the clock?","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"","options":["My crayons are in the box?","My crayons are in the box.","my crayons are in the box.","My crayons are in the box"],"answer":"My crayons are in the box.","explanation":"A telling sentence ends with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"الجملة الخبرية تنتهي بنقطة."},{"q":"","options":["What color is the map؟","what color is the map?","What color is the map?","What color is the map."],"answer":"What color is the map?","explanation":"Use the English question mark (?), not ؟.","explanation_ar":"استخدم علامة الاستفهام الإنجليزية."},{"q":"","options":["Are those your scissors.","are those your scissors?","Are those your scissors","Are those your scissors?"],"answer":"Are those your scissors?","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add a period (.) or a question mark (?).","items":[{"q":"Is the door open","options":[],"answer":"Is the door open?","explanation":"(add) → ?. A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ?. السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"The door is open","options":[],"answer":"The door is open.","explanation":"(add) → .. A telling sentence ends with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → .. الجملة الخبرية تنتهي بنقطة."},{"q":"Who is that boy","options":[],"answer":"Who is that boy?","explanation":"(add) → ?. A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ?. السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"That boy is my cousin","options":[],"answer":"That boy is my cousin.","explanation":"(add) → .. A telling sentence ends with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → .. الجملة الخبرية تنتهي بنقطة."},{"q":"How many chairs are there","options":[],"answer":"How many chairs are there?","explanation":"(add) → ?. A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ?. السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"the window is big.","options":[],"answer":"The window is big.","explanation":"the → The. Start the sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: the → The. ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the dialogue.","items":[{"q":"Omar: where is my ruler?","options":[],"answer":"Omar: Where is my ruler?","explanation":"where → Where. A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: where → Where. السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"Yusuf: It is on your desk Omar: Is it red? Yusuf: No, it is blue.","options":[],"answer":"Yusuf: It is on your desk. Omar: Is it red? Yusuf: No, it is blue.","explanation":"(add) → .. A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → .. السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"Yusuf: It is on your desk. Omar: Is it red. Yusuf: No, it is blue.","options":[],"answer":"Yusuf: It is on your desk. Omar: Is it red? Yusuf: No, it is blue.","explanation":". → ?. A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: . → ?. السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"Omar: Thank you? Yusuf is a good friend.","options":[],"answer":"Omar: Thank you. Yusuf is a good friend.","explanation":"? → .. A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: ? → .. السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"Omar: Thank you. yusuf is a good friend.","options":[],"answer":"Omar: Thank you. Yusuf is a good friend.","explanation":"yusuf → Yusuf. A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: yusuf → Yusuf. السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write questions and answers.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 questions about things in your classroom.","options":[],"answer":"Where is the map? Is the clock new?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses end punctuation: question mark (?) and period (.) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the answers to your questions.","options":[],"answer":"It is on the wall. Yes, it is.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses end punctuation: question mark (?) and period (.) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask your partner one question. Write his answer with a period.","options":[],"answer":"What is your favorite color? – My favorite color is blue.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses end punctuation: question mark (?) and period (.) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Builder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The teacher reads a word and a short clue.","Teams build the word with letter tiles in 30 seconds.","The team holds up the word; correct spelling = 1 point, with correct capital letter or punctuation where needed = 1 bonus point.","Continue until all words are used."],"data":[{"word":"pencil","clue":"a thing you use to write and draw"},{"word":"eraser","clue":"a small thing that takes away pencil marks"},{"word":"ruler","clue":"a long, flat thing for drawing straight lines"},{"word":"notebook","clue":"a book with empty pages for writing"},{"word":"crayon","clue":"a stick of colored wax for drawing"},{"word":"scissors","clue":"a tool with two blades for cutting paper"},{"word":"desk","clue":"a table where you sit and work at school"},{"word":"chair","clue":"a seat with a back for one person"},{"word":"board","clue":"a big flat surface on the wall for writing"},{"word":"clock","clue":"a thing on the wall that shows the time"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["Is the clock on the wall.","is the clock on the wall?","Is the clock on the wall?","Is the clock on the wall"],"answer":"Is the clock on the wall?","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"Which mark goes at the end? \"My desk is next to the window__\"","options":["؟",",","?","."],"answer":".","explanation":"A telling sentence ends with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"الجملة الخبرية تنتهي بنقطة."},{"q":"Which mark goes at the end? \"Whose bag is this__\"","options":["?",".","؟",","],"answer":"?","explanation":"Use the English question mark (?), not ؟.","explanation_ar":"استخدم علامة الاستفهام الإنجليزية."},{"q":"","options":["What is in your bag.","What is in your bag?","what is in your bag?","What is in your bag؟"],"answer":"What is in your bag?","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"Which one is a question?","options":["You are ready.","We are ready.","I am ready.","Are you ready?"],"answer":"Are you ready?","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"","options":["The scissors are sharp.","The scissors are sharp","The scissors are sharp?","the scissors are sharp."],"answer":"The scissors are sharp.","explanation":"A telling sentence ends with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"الجملة الخبرية تنتهي بنقطة."},{"q":"Which word often starts a question?","options":["The","This is","My","Where"],"answer":"Where","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"","options":["who is your teacher?","Who is your teacher","Who is your teacher?","Who is your teacher."],"answer":"Who is your teacher?","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"","options":["my pencil is under the desk.","My pencil is under the desk.","My pencil is under the desk?","My pencil is under the desk"],"answer":"My pencil is under the desk.","explanation":"A telling sentence ends with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"الجملة الخبرية تنتهي بنقطة."},{"q":"What is wrong? \"is this your eraser?\"","options":["Nothing is wrong.","It needs a capital I.","It needs ؟","It needs a period."],"answer":"It needs a capital I.","explanation":"Start the sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “In My Classroom” that shows end punctuation: question mark (?) and period (.) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “In My Classroom” that shows end punctuation: question mark (?) and period (.) in action"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Builder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Builder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Asking or Telling? Question Marks and Periods”. Let’s learn end punctuation: question mark (?) and period (.) together. A telling sentence gives information. It ends with a period (.): This is my ruler. A telling sentence gives information. It ends with a period (.): This is my ruler. A question asks for information. It ends with a question mark (?): Is this your ruler? Here are some examples. Where is my eraser? It is under the chair. What color is your bag? Be careful! Some learners say: “Is this your bag.” That’s not right. We say: “Is this your bag?.” It is a question → question mark. Quick check: \"Where is the map\" – telling or asking? Which mark? … Think! … Asking – a question mark. Great job! Now you can say: I can put a period at the end of a telling sentence.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS5","title":"Classroom Treasure Hunt: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to ask and answer questions about classroom objects.","Students will be able to write a short description of their desk with correct punctuation.","I can ask \"What's this?\" and \"Whose … are these?\" and answer them.","I can write about my desk with a, an and plurals."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح أسئلة عن أدوات الصف والإجابة عنها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة وصف قصير لطاولتهم بعلامات ترقيم صحيحة.","أستطيع أن أسأل What's this? وWhose … are these? وأجيب عنهما.","أستطيع أن أكتب عن طاولتي باستخدام a وan والجمع."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"pencil","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɛnsəl/","definition":"a thing you use to write and draw","arabic":"قلم رصاص","example":"Please sharpen your pencil.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"eraser","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪˈreɪsɚ/","definition":"a small thing that takes away pencil marks","arabic":"ممحاة","example":"This eraser smells like strawberries.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ruler","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrulɚ/","definition":"a long, flat thing for drawing straight lines","arabic":"مسطرة","example":"Use a ruler to draw the line.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"notebook","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈnoʊtˌbʊk/","definition":"a book with empty pages for writing","arabic":"دفتر","example":"Write the date in your notebook.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"desk","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɛsk/","definition":"a table where you sit and work at school","arabic":"مكتب / طاولة الطالب","example":"My desk is next to the door.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"chair","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tʃɛr/","definition":"a seat with a back for one person","arabic":"كرسي","example":"Push in your chair, please.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"board","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bɔrd/","definition":"a big flat surface on the wall for writing","arabic":"سبورة","example":"The teacher writes new words on the board.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"crayon","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkreɪˌɑn/","definition":"a stick of colored wax for drawing","arabic":"قلم تلوين شمعي","example":"The green crayon is broken.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"scissors","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsɪzɚz/","definition":"a tool with two blades for cutting paper","arabic":"مقص","example":"Be careful with the scissors!","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"glue stick","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡlu stɪk/","definition":"a stick of glue for sticking paper","arabic":"أصبع صمغ","example":"I need a glue stick for my poster.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"clock","pos":"noun","ipa":"/klɑk/","definition":"a thing on the wall that shows the time","arabic":"ساعة حائط","example":"The clock says ten o'clock.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"map","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mæp/","definition":"a picture that shows countries, cities and roads","arabic":"خريطة","example":"Find Taif on the map.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 3: a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words, colors and end punctuation.\nA good description says what things are, how many there are and what color they are.\n✔ a/an for one thing; -s/-es for many\n✔ this/these (near) and that/those (far)\n✔ color before the noun: a green ruler\n✔ period for telling sentences, question mark for questions","examples":["These are my crayons.","That is an old map.","I have a gray pencil case.","Two glue sticks are in my bag.","Is this your eraser?","Those chairs are new.","What's that next to the clock?","Her backpack is pink."],"common_errors":["✗ This is a pencils. → ✓ These are pencils. / This is a pencil. (One thing → this + a; many things → these + -s.)","✗ I have a eraser blue. → ✓ I have a blue eraser. (a before blue (consonant sound) and color before the noun.)","✗ Is that your bag. → ✓ Is that your bag? (Questions end with ?.)"],"arabic":"نجمع في هذا الدرس: a/an والجمع وthis/that/these/those والألوان وعلامات الترقيم.\nانتبه: a تتغير حسب الكلمة التالية مباشرة: an eraser لكن a blue eraser.\nالوصف الجيد يذكر الشيء ولونه وعدده."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Classroom Treasure Hunt: Language in Use”. Let’s learn a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U3-LS5 | Classroom Treasure Hunt: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Classroom treasure hunt: in teams, read clue cards (\"It is near the board. It is gray. What is it?\"), find the object and say \"That is the clock!\" or \"These are the crayons!\"","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 3: a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words, colors and end punctuation. A good description says what things are, how many there are and what color they are.","on_screen":"✔ a/an for one thing; -s/-es for many • ✔ this/these (near) and that/those (far) • ✔ color before the noun: a green ruler","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. These are my crayons. That is an old map. I have a gray pencil case.","on_screen":"These are my crayons. / That is an old map. / I have a gray pencil case.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “This is a pencils.” That’s not right. We say: “These are pencils. / This is a pencil.” One thing → this + a; many things → these + -s.","on_screen":"✗ This is a pencils.   ✓ These are pencils. / This is a pencil.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “I have a eraser blue.”? … Think! … It should be “I have a blue eraser.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"What's this?\" and \"Whose … are these?\" and answer them.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can ask \"What's this?\" and \"Whose … are these?\" and answer them.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نجمع في هذا الدرس: a/an والجمع وthis/that/these/those والألوان وعلامات الترقيم.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: This is a pencils. — الصحيح: These are pencils. / This is a pencil.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسأل What's this? وWhose … are these? وأجيب عنهما."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"My Desk – Adam","body":"This is my desk. It is next to the window.\nOn my desk is a notebook and an orange eraser.\nThese are my pencils. They are green and blue.\nThat is my bag on the chair. It is black.\nWhat is on your desk?","word_count":44,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Adam's text. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Adam's desk is next to the door.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Desk – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His eraser is orange.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Desk – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His pencils are red.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Desk – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His bag is on the chair.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Desk – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His bag is black.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Desk – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam has three notebooks on his desk.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Desk – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Adam has ___ orange eraser.","options":["a","some","an","two"],"answer":"an","explanation":"a/an for one thing (an before a vowel sound).","explanation_ar":"a/an للمفرد."},{"q":"___ are my pencils. (near)","options":["These","This","That","Those is"],"answer":"These","explanation":"this/these = near; that/those = far.","explanation_ar":"this/these للقريب، that/those للبعيد."},{"q":"We need three ___ for the art lesson.","options":["boxes","a box","box","boxs"],"answer":"boxes","explanation":"For many things, add -s or -es.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نضيف s أو es."},{"q":"My ruler is ___.","options":["yellows","the yellows","a yellow","yellow"],"answer":"yellow","explanation":"The color comes before the noun.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم."},{"q":"","options":["Whose scissors are these.","Whose scissors is these?","Who scissors are these?","Whose scissors are these?"],"answer":"Whose scissors are these?","explanation":"Telling → period; question → question mark.","explanation_ar":"الخبرية بنقطة والسؤال بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"Omar ___ my classmate.","options":["are","is","be","am"],"answer":"is","explanation":"a/an for one thing (an before a vowel sound).","explanation_ar":"a/an للمفرد."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Treasure hunt questions. Write the answers.","items":[{"q":"It is round. It is on the wall. It shows the time. What is it?","options":[],"answer":"It is the clock.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"They are long and thin. We write with them. What are they?","options":[],"answer":"They are pencils.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"It is big and white. The teacher writes on it. What is it?","options":[],"answer":"It is the board.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"They cut paper. They are always plural. What are they?","options":[],"answer":"They are scissors.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your own clue for a classmate.","options":[],"answer":"It is blue. It is in my bag. I write in it. (my notebook)","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write \"My Desk\".","items":[{"q":"Plan: list 4 things on your desk with colors and numbers.","options":[],"answer":"a red notebook, an eraser, two green pencils, a ruler","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 4–5 sentences about your desk. End with one question.","options":[],"answer":"This is my desk. On my desk is a red notebook and an eraser. These are my pencils. They are green. What is on your desk?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: a/an? -s/-es? . and ? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"a eraser\" to \"an eraser\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Quiz Show Challenge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams take turns choosing a category and a cue word.","Grammar: make a sentence with a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review). Words: give the meaning. Spelling: spell it. Write It!: write a sentence with correct punctuation.","Correct answers score 10 points; teams may steal a question another team misses.","The highest score after 8 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"pencil","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"eraser","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"ruler","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"notebook","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"desk","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"chair","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"board","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"crayon","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"scissors","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"glue stick","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"clock","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"map","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I want ___ apple.","options":["a","two","apples","an"],"answer":"an","explanation":"a/an for one thing (an before a vowel sound).","explanation_ar":"a/an للمفرد."},{"q":"___ is the school library. (far)","options":["Those","That","These","This are"],"answer":"That","explanation":"this/these = near; that/those = far.","explanation_ar":"this/these للقريب، that/those للبعيد."},{"q":"There are four ___ on the shelf.","options":["dictionarys","dictionary","a dictionary","dictionaries"],"answer":"dictionaries","explanation":"For many things, add -s or -es.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نضيف s أو es."},{"q":"","options":["I have a pink notebook.","I have pinks notebook.","I have a notebook pink.","I have an pink notebook."],"answer":"I have a pink notebook.","explanation":"The color comes before the noun.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم."},{"q":"Which mark ends this sentence? \"Are these your glue sticks__\"","options":["!","؟","?","."],"answer":"?","explanation":"Telling → period; question → question mark.","explanation_ar":"الخبرية بنقطة والسؤال بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"___ are my brothers over there.","options":["These is","That","This","Those"],"answer":"Those","explanation":"this/these = near; that/those = far.","explanation_ar":"this/these للقريب، that/those للبعيد."},{"q":"","options":["A boxes are on the floor.","Two box are on the floor.","Two boxes are on the floor.","Two boxs are on the floor."],"answer":"Two boxes are on the floor.","explanation":"For many things, add -s or -es.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نضيف s أو es."},{"q":"The scissors ___ in the drawer.","options":["are","be","am","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"For many things, add -s or -es.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نضيف s أو es."},{"q":"","options":["Is those an owl?","Is that an owl?","Is that an owl.","Is that a owl?"],"answer":"Is that an owl?","explanation":"a/an for one thing (an before a vowel sound).","explanation_ar":"a/an للمفرد."},{"q":"Which one is a telling sentence?","options":["Where is the clock?","What color is the clock?","The clock is gray.","Is the clock gray?"],"answer":"The clock is gray.","explanation":"Telling → period; question → question mark.","explanation_ar":"الخبرية بنقطة والسؤال بعلامة استفهام."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Children in teams holding clue cards during a classroom treasure hunt, one boy finding a box of crayons under a desk. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Children in teams holding clue cards during a classroom treasure hunt, one boy finding a box of crayons under a desk"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “In My Classroom”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “In My Classroom”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L01-U3-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Quiz Show Challenge”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Quiz Show Challenge"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS5-T1","script":"This is my desk. It is next to the window. On my desk is a notebook and an orange eraser. These are my pencils. They are green and blue. That is my bag on the chair. It is black. What is on your desk?","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U3-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Classroom Treasure Hunt: Language in Use”. Let’s learn a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words and end punctuation (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Classroom treasure hunt: in teams, read clue cards (\"It is near the board. It is gray. What is it?\"), find the object and say \"That is the clock!\" or \"These are the crayons!\" Today you use all of Unit 3: a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those, classroom words, colors and end punctuation. A good description says what things are, how many there are and what color they are. Here are some examples. These are my crayons. That is an old map. I have a gray pencil case. Be careful! Some learners say: “This is a pencils.” That’s not right. We say: “These are pencils. / This is a pencil.” One thing → this + a; many things → these + -s. Quick check: what is wrong with “I have a eraser blue.”? … Think! … It should be “I have a blue eraser.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"What's this?\" and \"Whose … are these?\" and answer them.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"I have ___ ruler and ___ eraser.","options":["a / an","a / a","an / an","an / a"],"answer":"a / an","explanation":"Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم an قبل الصوت المتحرك."},{"q":"She eats ___ orange every day.","options":["a","two","an","some"],"answer":"an","explanation":"Use an before a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم an قبل الصوت المتحرك."},{"q":"There are three ___ in the room.","options":["window","a window","windows","windowes"],"answer":"windows","explanation":"For two or more, add -s.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نضيف s."},{"q":"Two ___ are in the bag.","options":["lunches","lunchs","lunch","a lunch"],"answer":"lunches","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch or x, add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."},{"q":"","options":["I have two notebook.","I have a notebooks.","I have two notebooks.","I have two notebookes."],"answer":"I have two notebooks.","explanation":"Don't use a/an with plurals.","explanation_ar":"لا نستخدم a أو an مع الجمع."},{"q":"___ is my pencil. (in my hand)","options":["These","This","They","Those"],"answer":"This","explanation":"Near + one → this.","explanation_ar":"قريب ومفرد ← this."},{"q":"___ are the school gates. (far)","options":["These is","That","This","Those"],"answer":"Those","explanation":"Far + many → those.","explanation_ar":"بعيد وجمع ← those."},{"q":"What are ___? (near, many) – They're crayons.","options":["these","it","this","that"],"answer":"these","explanation":"Near + many → these.","explanation_ar":"قريب وجمع ← these."},{"q":"","options":["That is a big map.","These is a big map.","That are a big map.","Those is a big map."],"answer":"That is a big map.","explanation":"Far + one → that.","explanation_ar":"بعيد ومفرد ← that."},{"q":"","options":["Is these your books?","These are your books?","Are these your books?","Are this your books?"],"answer":"Are these your books?","explanation":"this/that + is; these/those + are.","explanation_ar":"this وthat مع is، وthese وthose مع are."},{"q":"Bandar cuts the card with ___.","options":["an eraser","a clock","a board","scissors"],"answer":"scissors","explanation":"Think about what we use the thing for.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في استخدام الأداة."},{"q":"Look at the ___. It is two o'clock.","options":["crayon","desk","map","clock"],"answer":"clock","explanation":"Think about what we use the thing for.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في استخدام الأداة."},{"q":"","options":["I want an purple crayon.","I want a purple crayon.","I want a crayon purple.","I want a purples crayon."],"answer":"I want a purple crayon.","explanation":"The color comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"اللون قبل الاسم ولا يُجمع."},{"q":"These scissors ___ sharp.","options":["is","be","are","am"],"answer":"are","explanation":"scissors / glasses / pants are always plural → are, a pair of.","explanation_ar":"هذه الكلمات جمع دائمًا."},{"q":"We draw straight lines with a ___.","options":["glue stick","chair","notebook","ruler"],"answer":"ruler","explanation":"Think about what we use the thing for.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في استخدام الأداة."},{"q":"Can I have the eraser, please? – ___","options":["I'm hungry.","Here you are.","Good evening.","Goodbye."],"answer":"Here you are.","explanation":"Ask politely: Can I have…, please?","explanation_ar":"اطلب بأدب: Can I have…, please?"},{"q":"","options":["Where is my bag?","where is my bag?","Where is my bag؟","Where is my bag."],"answer":"Where is my bag?","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"","options":["my bag is under the desk.","My bag is under the desk.","My bag is under the desk?","My bag is under the desk"],"answer":"My bag is under the desk.","explanation":"A telling sentence ends with a period (.).","explanation_ar":"الجملة الخبرية تنتهي بنقطة."},{"q":"Which mark goes at the end? \"What color is your chair__\"","options":[",",".","؟","?"],"answer":"?","explanation":"Use the English question mark (?), not ؟.","explanation_ar":"استخدم علامة الاستفهام الإنجليزية."},{"q":"Choose the question.","options":["The door is brown.","Is the door open?","The door is open.","Open the door."],"answer":"Is the door open?","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"","options":["Whose crayons are these?","whose crayons are these?","Who crayons are these?","Whose crayons are these."],"answer":"Whose crayons are these?","explanation":"A question ends with a question mark (?).","explanation_ar":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for \"My Desk\":","options":["On my desk is a orange eraser.","On my desk an orange eraser.","On my desk is an eraser orange.","On my desk is an orange eraser."],"answer":"On my desk is an orange eraser.","explanation":"Use a before a consonant sound.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم a قبل الصوت الساكن."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"these is my crayons.\"","options":["This are my crayons.","These is my crayons.","These are my crayons.","these are my crayons?"],"answer":"These are my crayons.","explanation":"this/that + is; these/those + are.","explanation_ar":"this وthat مع is، وthese وthose مع are."},{"q":"Choose the correct pair:","options":["an map – two mapes","a map – two maps","a map – two mapes","a maps – two map"],"answer":"a map – two maps","explanation":"For two or more, add -s.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نضيف s."}],"theme_ar":"في صفي","essential_question_ar":"ماذا نحتاج لنتعلّم جيدًا في صفنا؟","can_do":"I can name classroom things with a, an and plurals, and point to things near and far with this, that, these and those.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أسمّي أدوات الصف باستخدام a وan والجمع، وأشير إلى الأشياء القريبة والبعيدة باستخدام this وthat وthese وthose."});
